<title>GERMANY: Pan-German Dec industry orders fall 1.4 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>Pan-German Dec industry orders fall 1.4 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The economics ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN INDUSTRY ORDERS  Dec 96     Nov 96     Dec 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change	  -1.4	 -0.5	 -1.3</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +2.4	 +2.6	  n/a</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		96.7	 98.1	 94.4</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional and expressed in volume terms. Year-on-year changes are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank data. @</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following month-on-month details:</p>
<p>				     Dec 96     Nov 96    Dec 96 index</p>
<p> Total domestic orders	  -0.4	 +0.1	  90.1</p>
<p> Total foreign orders	   -2.7	 -1.5	 110.0</p>
<p> Intermediate goods	     +1.3	 -1.2	 102.6</p>
<p> Of which: domestic	     +1.7	 -0.9	  96.0</p>
<p>	     foreign		+0.6	 -1.5	 117.7</p>
<p> Capital goods		    -6.7	 +1.7	  93.2</p>
<p> Of which: domestic	     -4.9	 +3.2	  86.7</p>
<p>	     foreign		-8.6	 -0.5	 104.1</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables     +2.0	 -2.9	  88.6</p>
<p> Of which: domestic	     +1.6	 -2.8	  80.5</p>
<p>	     foreign		+2.2	 -3.2	 105.4 @</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Nov/Dec 96 with Sept/Oct 96:</p>
<p> Industrial orders		     unch</p>
<p> Domestic orders			 +1.0</p>
<p> Foreign orders			  -1.0</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    +0.5</p>
<p> Capital goods			   unch</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	    -1.0 @</p>
<p>Two month comparison Nov/Dec 96 with Nov/Dec 95:</p>
<p> Industrial orders		     -0.4</p>
<p> Domestic orders			 -3.7</p>
<p> Foreign orders			  +5.2</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    +4.4</p>
<p> Capital goods			   -5.0</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	    -3.4</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097-150</p>
</text>
